# Current MCP examples. Contracts and source-write workflow: docs/README.md and docs/write-operations.md.
# Full access publishes nineteen tools; explicit read-only access publishes eleven.
@base = http://127.0.0.1:5000

### Initialize the MCP connection (no TIA attachment)
POST {{base}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"initialize","params":{"protocolVersion":"2025-03-26","capabilities":{},"clientInfo":{"name":"http-examples","version":"1"}}}

### List the tools published by the server's access profile
POST {{base}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"method":"tools/list"}

### Passive bridge status (no TIA attachment)
POST {{base}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":3,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"get_status","arguments":{}}}

### Discover running TIA processes (no attachment)
POST {{base}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":4,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"list_tia_processes","arguments":{}}}

### Passive dashboard snapshot (no process discovery or attachment)
GET {{base}}/api/dashboard/dashboard

### Passive dashboard log window
GET {{base}}/api/dashboard/logs?after=0&generation=0

# Browser dashboard POST actions and its MCP calls use X-Tia-Dashboard: 1.
# External MCP clients do not need this dashboard-origin header.
